  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ohio recorded $54.9M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $50.1M in FY2027 to date. The state has seen much larger annual totals in recent years: FY22 obligations were $7.8B, FY23 obligations were $10.1B, FY24 obligations were $9B, FY25 obligations were $9.8B, and FY26 obligations were $7.9B. Award activity for FY2027 to date shows 298 awards with an average award size of $184K. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry in FY2027 to date with $16.1M. LC FLUHARTY CONSTRUCTION LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $14.9M. The current-year data shows a concentrated set of buyers, industries, and vendors that account for most obligations so far in FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Ohio this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $50.1M in FY2027 to date. The total for Ohio is $54.9M, so VA spending accounts for the majority of current-year obligations. Award activity shows 298 awards and an average award size of $184K. Prior fiscal years were much larger, for example FY26 obligations were $7.9B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate FY2027 federal contracting in Ohio?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads industries with $16.1M. Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing follows with $10.6M, and Couriers and Express Delivery Services and Electric Power Distribution each have $2.9M. LC FLUHARTY CONSTRUCTION LLC is the top vendor with $14.9M, followed by CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC with $9.8M and CONSTELLATION NEWENERGY, INC. with $2.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Ohio?",
      "a": "Ohio received $54.9M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Award activity in FY2027 to date includes 298 awards and an average award size of $184K. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year and prior fiscal years were larger: FY22 was $7.8B, FY23 was $10.1B, FY24 was $9B, FY25 was $9.8B, and FY26 was $7.9B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Ohio?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awards the most contracts in Ohio, obligating $50.1M in FY2027 to date. The next-largest buyers in FY2027 to date are National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $1.8M, Social Security Administration with $1.4M, and General Services Administration with $1.1M. Department of the Treasury obligated $996K, Department of Justice obligated $472K, Environmental Protection Agency obligated $323K, Department of Labor obligated $165K."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Ohio?",
      "a": "LC FLUHARTY CONSTRUCTION LLC is the largest federal contractor in Ohio in FY2027 to date with $14.9M. CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC follows with $9.8M, CONSTELLATION NEWENERGY, INC. has $2.9M, UNITED PARCEL SERVICE CO. has $2.7M, and ARROW ARC LLC has $2.2M. Other top vendors include OHIO AMBULANCE SOLUTIONS, LLC with $2.1M and CINCOM SYSTEMS, INC. with $1.4M."
